        "pacing_notes": "This is a climb in 4/5 parts: The first step sections are just as you enter into the park where it tilts up to about 8-9% from the tracks to the field. The climb then levels off midway through the park and all the way through the hamlet at the other end. Right after the parking lot and Joncaire, the road gradually tilts up for a long drag to the railroad tracks, but almost immediately afterward, the road curves left into 3 blocks of 12+% spitting you out directly onto 5th.",
        "summary": "This is one of the most trafficked bike routes in the city, getting you from Oakland to the Eliza Furnace",
