        "pacing_notes": "Unless you're coming down from Greenfield, the climb starts with a dangerous 9% punch round a slight, blind bend (the bike lane starts just after it's needed). Instead of continuing up the hill, you make a left onto a bridge across the turnpike. The climb then becomes one of the few \"draftable\" climbs in the region, but make sure to save something for the end. When you make the final curve into the neighborhood at the top, you need to punch through a short steep block, as the first road is one way.",
        "summary": "A very gradual climb once you make it to the bridge. A very fun descent if taken the otherway",
        "related_segments": []
    },
