        "pacing_notes": "Climbing out of the west end, you have a block of 10%. Despite the concrete wall in front of you, this is the steepest part of the climb. You turn left to a very consistent 5-6% as the road winds its way around the hill. The road pinches up a bit (and the shoulders shrink) as you get back into some housing, before falling back down to a false flat. You are then presented with a choice of heading left, straight, or right - each option is basically the same length and gradient and all are very consistent.",
        "summary": "A very easy climb that is extremely difficult to get to with the current cycling infrastructure. Fairly wide shoulders along most of the route",
